# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy to `.env.local`. Every value here is OPTIONAL — the site runs without it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Public origin, used for the share preview, canonical links and calendar files.
# Optional: when unset, the origin is read from the incoming request, so a link
# shared on WhatsApp previews correctly on any hostname. Set it once you know the
# final domain and it will be preferred over the request.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://invite.example.com

# Password for the hidden /admin guest list. If unset, /admin stays locked and the
# read/delete API returns 401 — nobody can read your guest list without it.
# Generate one with:  node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(24).toString('base64url'))"
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Comma-separated list of extra origins allowed to POST an RSVP. Leave unset for
# same-origin only, which is all the invitation needs.
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=

# Where the RSVP replies are written. Only used when no Redis store is
# configured below. Defaults to ./data/rsvp.json.
# MUST point at persistent storage on a host with an ephemeral filesystem
# (Vercel, Netlify, most container platforms) or replies will disappear on
# redeploy.
# RSVP_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/invitation

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RSVP STORE -- the durable option, and the one to use on Vercel.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# On Vercel the filesystem is read-only, which is why replies used to return a
# 500. Create a free Upstash Redis database (or a Vercel KV store) and set BOTH
# a URL and a token. With both set, replies go to Redis and survive redeploys;
# with neither set, the JSON file above is used.
#
# Create one at https://console.upstash.com  ->  Create Database, then copy the
# REST credentials. The two naming conventions below are both accepted, because
# a Vercel KV store and an Upstash database hand out different variable names.
#
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://eu1-xxx.upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=...
#
# KV_REST_API_URL=https://kv-xxx.upstash.io     # Vercel KV marketplace
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=...
#
# Set only one half and /admin will say so: the store falls back to a local file
# and replies are silently lost on the next deploy.